        <!-- SECTION 2: ATTENDANCE & DISCIPLINARY BENCHMARKS -->
        <div style="margin-bottom: 64px;">
          <div class="section-kicker">Attendance & discipline</div>
          <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size: 36px; margin-bottom: 24px;">2. ATTENDANCE & CITIZENSHIP RULES</h2>

          <div style="background: var(--cream-card); border: 1px solid var(--border-light); border-radius: 4px; padding: 36px;">
            <ul class="op-list">
              <li>${ICONS.diamondBullet} <span><strong>Game-Day Attendance Mandate:</strong> Student-athletes must attend all scheduled classes on the day of a competition. Any unexcused absence, truancy, or skipping class during periods 1 through 6 results in an immediate game-day suspension.</span></li>
              <li>${ICONS.diamondBullet} <span><strong>School Suspension Threshold:</strong> An athlete cannot have been suspended from school more than <strong>once</strong> during their high school career. Receiving a second formal in-school or out-of-school suspension triggers automatic, permanent athletic disqualification from all sports teams.</span></li>
              <li>${ICONS.diamondBullet} <span><strong>Physical & Concussion Clearance:</strong> Participation is prohibited until a fully completed CIF physical examination form (signed by a licensed M.D. or D.O.), proof of insurance, and baseline ImPACT concussion testing are uploaded and verified by the Athletic Trainer.</span></li>
              <li>${ICONS.diamondBullet} <span><strong>Practice Attendance & Tardiness:</strong> Missing more than 3 consecutive practices without an excused medical doctor's note or prior head coach approval results in mandatory suspension from the next competitive fixture.</span></li>
              <li>${ICONS.diamondBullet} <span><strong>Locker Room & Equipment Stewardship:</strong> Intentional misuse, theft, or neglect of school athletic gear, weight room equipment, or uniforms results in financial restitution holds and suspension until resolved.</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 3: OFFICIAL CIF CONDITIONS & RULES -->
        <div style="margin-bottom: 64px;">
          <div class="section-kicker">CIF Southern Section bylaws</div>
          <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size: 36px; margin-bottom: 24px;">3. OFFICIAL CIF CONDITIONS & STATE BYLAWS</h2>

          <div style="background: var(--navy-main); color: #fff; border-radius: 4px; padding: 40px; box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(7, 22, 44, 0.15); border-left: 6px solid var(--red);">
            <h4 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 26px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 16px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #fff;">Mandatory California Interscholastic Federation Rules</h4>
            <p style="font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 24px;">
              San Clemente Beach High School is a voluntary member school of the CIF Southern Section and strictly enforces all state blue-book bylaws:
            </p>

            <ul style="list-style: none; display: grid; gap: 16px;">
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9);">
                <span style="color: var(--red); font-weight: 800; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 18px;">[200]</span>
                <span><strong>Minimum Enrollment & Progress:</strong> Students must maintain enrollment in at least 20 semester credits (four robust courses) and make standard progress toward high school graduation.</span>
              </li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9);">
                <span style="color: var(--powder-blue); font-weight: 800; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 18px;">[510]</span>
                <span><strong>Transfer & Residence Validity:</strong> Athletic eligibility for transfer students requires a verified valid change of residential address or approved hardship waiver. Undue influence or athletic motivation in school enrollment results in loss of eligibility.</span>
              </li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9);">
                <span style="color: var(--red); font-weight: 800; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 18px;">[600]</span>
                <span><strong>Eight-Semester Rule:</strong> High school athletic eligibility is strictly restricted to eight consecutive semesters following initial entry into the 9th grade.</span>
              </li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9);">
                <span style="color: var(--powder-blue); font-weight: 800; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 18px;">[1100]</span>
                <span><strong>Outside Team Competition:</strong> During a designated CIF sport season, a varsity athlete may not compete on an outside club or showcase team in that same sport without prior written waiver approval from the Athletic Director.</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 4: SCHOOL EXPECTATIONS & OFFENSES -->
        <div style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
          <div class="section-kicker">Sportsmanship & character code</div>
          <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size: 36px; margin-bottom: 24px;">4. SCHOOL EXPECTATIONS & UNSPORTSMANLIKE OFFENSES</h2>

          <div class="op-card accent-red" style="margin-bottom: 28px; padding: 32px;">
            <div class="op-card-kicker">THE MARLINS CREED</div>
            <h4 style="font-size: 22px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Respect for Competition & Community</h4>
            <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; color: #273852;">
              All Marlins players, coaches, and student supporters must respect competition, officials, opponents, and facilities. We win with absolute humility and lose with unwavering grace. Trash talking, disrespecting game officials, or taunting opposing student sections violates the core character of San Clemente Beach Athletics.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div style="background: var(--cream-card); border: 1px solid var(--border-light); border-radius: 4px; padding: 36px;">
            <h4 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 24px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px; text-transform: uppercase;">Serious Unsportsmanlike Offenses</h4>
            <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 20px; font-style: italic;">
              * Note: These are serious unsportsmanlike offenses—explicitly excluding routine competitive banter, emotional intensity, or ordinary on-field game chatter.
            </p>

            <ul class="op-list">
              <li>${ICONS.diamondBullet} <span><strong>Physical Assault or Retaliation:</strong> Striking, shoving, spitting, or attempting to physically harm an opponent, referee, athletic trainer, or spectator outside normal sport mechanics.</span></li>
              <li>${ICONS.diamondBullet} <span><strong>Hate Speech & Discriminatory Harassment:</strong> Uttering racial, ethnic, religious, disability, or sexual orientation slurs directed at any participant or official.</span></li>
              <li>${ICONS.diamondBullet} <span><strong>Intentional Equipment Tampering:</strong> Modifying bats, sticks, padding, or protective gear to create an illegal competitive advantage or risk player safety.</span></li>
              <li>${ICONS.diamondBullet} <span><strong>Flagrant Disqualification Ejection:</strong> Receiving a direct ejection, match disqualification, or red card for malicious unsportsmanlike conduct, referee intimidation, or instigating bench-clearing altercations.</span></li>
              <li>${ICONS.diamondBullet} <span><strong>Vandalism or Hostile Property Destruction:</strong> Causing intentional damage to opposing school gymnasiums, locker rooms, athletic fields, or team transportation buses during away travel.</span></li>
            </ul>

            <div style="margin-top: 28px; background: rgba(216, 30, 40, 0.05); border: 1px solid rgba(216, 30, 40, 0.2); border-left: 4px solid var(--red); padding: 22px; border-radius: 4px;">
              <div style="font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--red); margin-bottom: 4px;">DISQUALIFICATION RULE</div>
              <p style="font-size: 14.5px; color: #273852; line-height: 1.65;">
                If a student-athlete violates any of these serious unsportsmanlike offenses more than <strong>1 time throughout their high school career</strong>, they are permanently disqualified from all athletic participation at San Clemente Beach High School.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
  `;
